People can be created or updated via a POST method to [https://api.custify.com/people](https://api.custify.com/people), which accepts a JSON object describing the people. People not found via email or user_id will be created, and those found will be updated if one of the attributes contains a new value or if you add a new attribute.

Note that the following lookup order applies when updating people: first `id` (Custify internal ID), then `user_id` (your internal ID of the person), then `email`. This results in the following logic:
- `id` is matched: the `user_id` and `email` will be updated if they"re sent
- `user_id` match: the `email` will be updated, the `id` is not updated
- `email` match where no `user_id` set on the matching user: the `user_id` will be set to the value sent in the request, the `id` is not updated
- `email` match where there is a `user_id` set on the matching user: a new unique record with new `id` will be created if a new value for `user_id` is sent in the request.

### Associate people with a company
The assignment of people to companies should be done as soon as possible in your process; ideally right after creating the person entry. Once people are assigned to a company, the events they generate are also associated with that company.
To associate a company with a customer, send a POST request with the following JSON body:
```json
{
  "id": "531ee472cce572a6ec000005",
  "companies": [
    {
      "company_id" : "366"
    }
  ]
}
```
where `company_id` is *your internal ID* of the company and was specified through the company API call before. If you want to use the Custify internal ID, send a POST with the following JSON body:
```json
{
  "id": "531ee472cce572a6ec000005",
  "companies": [
    {
      "id" : "531ee472cce572a6ec000006"
    }
  ]
}
```

### Remove people from a company
To remove people from a company, send a POST request with the following JSON body:
```json
{
  "id": "531ee472cce572a6ec000005",
  "companies": [
    {
      "company_id" : "3",
      "remove" : true
    }
  ]
}
```
where `company_id` is *your internal ID* of the company and was specified through the company API call before. If you want to use the Custify internal ID, send a POST with the following JSON body:
```json
{
  "id": "531ee472cce572a6ec000005",
  "companies": [
    {
      "id" : "531ee472cce572a6ec000006",
      "remove" : true
    }
  ]
}
```

Companies can be created or updated via a POST to https://api.custify.com/company, which accepts a JSON object describing the company.
Companies are looked up via `id` or `company_id` - if it's not found via both parameters, the new company will be created. If a company is found, it will be updated.

Note that the `company_id` field itself cannot be updated through the API.

When submitting custom attributes of type `User` you can specify the Custify internal ID of the user or the email address. Examples:
```json
{
  "company_id": "1",
  "custom_attributes": {
    "user_type_field": "531ee472cce572a6ec000006"
  }
}
```
or

```json
{
  "company_id": "1",
  "custom_attributes": {
    "user_type_field": "john.doe@example.com"
  }
}
```

### Associate a company with another company
Once a company is assigned to another company, the events generated by the people that are part of the "child" company are also associated with the "parent" company.
To associate a company with another company, send a POST request with the following JSON body:
```json
{
  "company_id": "1",
  "parent_companies": [
    {
      "company_id" : "2"
    }
  ]
}
```
where `company_id` is *your internal ID* of the company and was specified through the company API call. If you want to use the Custify internal ID, send a POST with the following JSON body:
```json
{
  "company_id": "1",
  "parent_companies": [
    {
      "id" : "531ee472cce572a6ec000006"
    }
  ]
}
```

### Remove a company from 'parent_companies' of another company
To remove a company from 'parent_companies' of another company, send a POST request with the following JSON body:
```json
{
  "company_id": "1",
  "parent_companies": [
    {
      "company_id" : "2",
      "remove" : true
    }
  ]
}
```
where `company_id` is *your internal ID* of the company and was specified through the company API call. If you want to use the Custify internal ID, send a POST with the following JSON body:
```json
{
  "company_id": "1",
  "companies": [
    {
      "id" : "531ee472cce572a6ec000006",
      "remove" : true
    }
  ]
}
```

### Insert/update a field of type 'Currency'
To insert/update a field of type 'Currency', send a POST request with the following JSON body:
```json
{
  "company_id": "1",
  "custom_attributes": {
      "currency_field": {
        "value": 100,
        "currency": "USD"
      }
  }
}
```

